  "aiContextParagraph": "The political landscape in Punjab is shifting as the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) and the Shiromani Akali Dal (SAD) have reconciled after a six-year separation, aiming to consolidate their respective bases for the 2027 state elections. This reunion has sparked criticism from the Congress party, with leaders questioning the rationale behind the alliance given previous disagreements on agricultural policies and other state issues. Concurrently, reports indicate that jailed hardliner Amritpal Singh and various breakaway Akali factions are in negotiations to form a separate regional and 'Panthic' grouping. There is speculation that this emerging coalition could also involve the Bahujan Samaj Party. As political maneuvering intensifies, Amritpal Singh is expected to target seats currently held by the Aam Aadmi Party, particularly in the Malwa and Majha regions, as the state prepares for its upcoming electoral cycle.",
